-- Tests for Chapter 17 of the Penal Code 1871 (Offences against property),
-- ss 378-462, over pc-property-theft, pc-property-trust, pc-property-cheating
-- and pc-property-mischief.
--
-- Expected values come from the Code: every Illustration that can be stated
-- on the atoms is an #ASSERT, cited on the line above ("-- s 378 illus (a)").
-- Boundary cases for every threshold (5 persons, 20 tons) are on the helpers.
-- Charge texts: the two reported charges the reference row pins (Lewis
-- Christine, s 420; the Illustration (q) bank transfer, s 379) are asserted
-- byte for byte, so this encoding reproduces what the charge generator shows
-- today. An assertion that fails is a finding, never an expected value to edit.
--
-- Fixtures are complete record literals: every leaf not named TRUE is FALSE,
-- which is also how the charge generator completes a partial record.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-property-theft`
IMPORT `pc-property-trust`
IMPORT `pc-property-cheating`
IMPORT `pc-property-mischief`

§ `Fixtures shared by every family`

`the particulars` MEANS Particulars WITH
    accused            IS "Tan Ah Kow"
    date               IS "the 1st day of June 2026"
    time               IS "9.00 pm"
    place              IS "Blk 1 Toa Payoh Lorong 1"
    `co-accused`       IS ""
    `common intention` IS FALSE

